"""Leading with AI (Leadership Edition), Session 2: AI that predicts from your data.  Pilot session, written 11 to 12 November 2026.

The pattern for every concept session: recall and a hook with a real case; the idea as a ladder of pictures with no maths; the six-industry
tour and three case stories; a recorded demonstration; your people; questions to ask; the portfolio hands-on; the decision; the take-away.

Cases (research/*.md): BNK-03 Numida (hook and tour), TEL-06 Airtel Money and GnuGrid CRB, AGR-03 Apollo Agriculture, MFG-03 Coca-Cola
suggested orders (tour and case), HLT-02 Jacaranda Health, PUB-07 Togo Novissi (tour), TEL-01 M-Shwari with TEL-02 for its catch (case),
AGR-05 Gro Intelligence (failure case), TEL-04 Safaricom petitions (who owns the decision).
Demonstration: the recorded runs in demo_runs/s02/ (learn_run.py; scikit-learn 1.9.1; recorded 5 November 2026, re-run 11 November 2026
with identical results plus the fold-by-fold scores; see RUN_RECORD_2026-11-11.md).  The 240 expense claims are FICTIONAL.  The 40 customer
messages belong to Nile Valley Foods, the fictional course company.  Borrower tables, scores and shop entries marked illustrative are invented.
"""

